  "result": "- **Schedule: correct.** `config/prod.yaml:2` sets `session_gc_schedule: \"*/10 * * * *\"`, so `session-gc` runs every 10 minutes.\n- **Idle rule: correct.** `auth/session_gc.py:3` sets `IDLE_LIMIT` to 30 minutes. `collect` deletes rows where `last_seen_at` is older than that.\n- **Time zone mismatch: wrong.** `collect` builds `cutoff` with `datetime.now(timezone.utc)` at `auth/session_gc.py:7`. The column `last_seen_at` is `timestamptz` in `auth/schema.sql:4`. Both sides are timezone-aware, so the comparison is correct.\n\nThe case is not a clock bug. `session-gc` reads the right time and finds a stale `last_seen_at`. That value is stale because `edge-proxy/session.py:8` skips `auth_client.touch` while `touch_on_request` is false in `config/prod.yaml:1`.\n\n**Close.** One item is still open from my last message. Aelita recommends turning on `touch_on_request` in production, because it is a one-line config change and the touch code already exists. Do we turn it on, or move the touch into `auth-service`?",
